cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Angelica in your work, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "Angelica"
abstract: >
  Angelica is an open-source platform for steady pipe network simulation. It
  computes nodal pressures, flow rates, temperatures, and global mass/energy
  balances in networks of pipes, fittings, pumps, and inline heat sources. The
  hydraulic solver uses a pressure-correction algorithm (modified SIMPLE) with
  Colebrook-White, Hazen-Williams, or Poiseuille closures. Current solver modes
  include isothermal incompressible, non-isothermal incompressible, compressible
  gas, and black-oil three-phase flow. A graphical network editor is included.
authors:
